## Code Organization Rules

### Controllers
- **Location**: `src/main/java/com/todoai/controller/`
- **Naming**: `{Resource}Controller.java`
- **Annotation**: `@RestController`
- **Base Route**: `@RequestMapping("/api/v1/{resource}")`
- **Methods**: Use `@GetMapping`, `@PostMapping`, `@PutMapping`, `@DeleteMapping`
- **Validation**: Add `@Valid` to DTO parameters
- **Documentation**: JavaDoc for all public methods

**Example**:
```java
@RestController
@RequestMapping("/api/v1/todo")
@Slf4j
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class TodoController {
    private final TodoService service;

    @GetMapping("/list")
    public ResponseEntity<List<TodoDTO>> getAll() {
        return ResponseEntity.ok(service.findAll());
    }
}
```

### Services
- **Location**: `src/main/java/com/todoai/service/`
- **Naming**: `{Resource}Service.java`
- **Annotation**: `@Service`
- **Injection**: `@RequiredArgsConstructor` with constructor parameters
- **Transactions**: `@Transactional` for write operations
- **Logic**: All business logic here, not in controllers

**Example**:
```java
@Service
@Slf4j
@RequiredArgsConstructor
public class TodoService {
    private final TodoRepository repository;

    @Transactional
    public TodoDTO create(TodoDTO dto) {
        Todo entity = mapper.toEntity(dto);
        Todo saved = repository.save(entity);
        return mapper.toDTO(saved);
    }
}
```

### Repositories
- **Location**: `src/main/java/com/todoai/repository/`
- **Naming**: `{Resource}Repository.java`
- **Extends**: `JpaRepository<Entity, ID>`
- **Methods**: Use Spring Data JPA query derivation
- **Logic**: Data access only, no business logic

**Example**:
```java
public interface TodoRepository extends JpaRepository<Todo, Long> {
    List<Todo> findByCompletedFalse();
    List<Todo> findByCompletedTrue();
}
```

### Models (Entities)
- **Location**: `src/main/java/com/todoai/model/`
- **Naming**: `{Resource}.java`
- **Annotation**: `@Entity`
- **ID**: `@Id @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)`
- **Timestamps**: `createdAt`, `updatedAt` with `@PrePersist`, `@PreUpdate`
- **Lombok**: Use `@Data`, `@NoArgsConstructor`, `@AllArgsConstructor`

**Example**:
```java
@Entity
@Table(name = "todos")
@Data
@NoArgsConstructor
@AllArgsConstructor
public class Todo {
    @Id
    @GeneratedValue(strategy = GenerationType.IDENTITY)
    private Long id;

    @Column(nullable = false)
    private String title;

    @PrePersist
    protected void onCreate() {
        createdAt = LocalDateTime.now(ZoneId.of("UTC"));
    }
}
```

### DTOs (Data Transfer Objects)
- **Location**: `src/main/java/com/todoai/dto/`
- **Naming**: `{Resource}DTO.java`
- **Validation**: Include Jakarta Validation annotations
- **Lombok**: Use `@Data`, `@NoArgsConstructor`, `@AllArgsConstructor`
- **Purpose**: API input/output, not entities

**Example**:
```java
@Data
@NoArgsConstructor
@AllArgsConstructor
public class TodoDTO {
    private Long id;

    @NotBlank(message = "Title is required")
    @Size(min = 1, max = 255)
    private String title;
}
```

### Configuration
- **Location**: `src/main/java/com/todoai/config/`
- **Naming**: `{Component}Config.java`
- **Annotation**: `@Configuration`
- **Purpose**: Spring beans, database config, etc.

---

## Naming Conventions

| Element | Convention | Example |
|---------|-----------|---------|
| **Classes** | PascalCase | `TodoController`, `TodoService` |
| **Methods** | camelCase | `getTodoById()`, `createTodo()` |
| **Variables** | camelCase | `todoList`, `savedEntity` |
| **Constants** | UPPER_SNAKE_CASE | `DEFAULT_PAGE_SIZE`, `MAX_RETRIES` |
| **Packages** | lowercase.dot | `com.todoai.controller` |
| **Database Tables** | lowercase_plural | `todos`, `reminders` |
| **Database Columns** | lowercase_snake | `created_at`, `updated_at` |

---

## REST API Standards

### URL Patterns
```
GET    /api/v1/todo/list              - List all todos
GET    /api/v1/todo/list/active       - List active todos
GET    /api/v1/todo/list/completed    - List completed todos
GET    /api/v1/todo/{id}              - Get single todo
POST   /api/v1/todo                   - Create todo
PUT    /api/v1/todo/{id}              - Update todo
DELETE /api/v1/todo/{id}              - Delete todo
```

### HTTP Status Codes
- `200 OK` - GET, PUT success
- `201 Created` - POST success
- `204 No Content` - DELETE success
- `400 Bad Request` - Invalid input
- `404 Not Found` - Resource not found
- `500 Server Error` - Server error

### Response Format
```json
{
  "id": 1,
  "title": "My Todo",
  "description": "Description",
  "completed": false,
  "createdAt": "2026-04-03T10:30:00Z",
  "updatedAt": "2026-04-03T10:30:00Z"
}
```

